   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate both sides of \\( \\cos\\left(g(x)\\right) = \\frac{4 x + 7}{9} \\) with respect to x. The chain rule on the left gives \\( -\\sin\\left(g(x)\\right) \\cdot g'(x) = \\frac{4}{9} \\).",
         "rule_named": "chain rule on the identity f(g(x)) = x"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Express the trigonometric factor in x by the Pythagorean identity, with the positive root because the sine is not negative on this branch: \\( \\sin\\left(g(x)\\right) = \\sqrt{1 - \\cos^{2}\\left(g(x)\\right)} = \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac{4 x}{9} + \\frac{7}{9}\\right)^{2}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "Pythagorean identity on the principal branch"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Solve for the derivative: \\( g'(x) = - \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{81 - \\left(4 x + 7\\right)^{2}}} \\).",
